{
  "about": "What Semitone knows about specific plug-ins: which controls matter, in plain words, and what they need to be heard. Every control here was measured on the installed plug-in with its default patch on 2026-11-06. role is what a producer move asks for (volume, filter, reverb, delay, drive) or an extra shown in Automation (attack, release, resonance, timbre, sustain). on: a switch that must be on, which a move turns on for its own sections. idle: the value that sounds like the effect being off, used as the start when the switch was off. set: other controls to hold while switched on. max: the highest value a move may use. faint: little or no change on the default patch, so a real patch may be needed. Names can change with a plug-in's version: a control that isn't found falls back to matching by name.",
  "maps": [
